[1m[38;5;231mWhere should the userId persist in the browser?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mlocalStorage (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mSurvives browser restarts and is shared across tabs, matching "it should persist". Readable by any script on the [39m
     [38;5;246mpage, so it needs an explicit logout path that clears it.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m sessionStorage
     [38;5;246mScoped to one tab and cleared when it closes. Smallest exposure window, but the user re-authenticates in every new
[39m     [38;5;246mtab and it does not survive restarts.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m In-memory only for now
     [38;5;246mHold identity in the module with no persistence yet. Zero storage exposure; loses the identity on every page load,
[39m     [38;5;246mso it does not meet the persist requirement.[39m
